        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "2074e3f2-974e-5e50-82ec-671bfaf8cf19",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: USS Barataria, USCGC Barataria\n- Organizations: United States Coast Guard, United States, Soviet Union\n- Events: Cuban Missile Crisis, Vietnam War\n- Concepts: October Crisis, Caribbean Crisis, Missile Scare\n\nFacts:\n- From 1949 to 1969, USS Barataria was transferred to the United States Coast Guard and served in commission as the cutter USCGC Barataria, designated WAVP-381 and later WHEC-381.\n- From October 16 to October 28, 1962, the Cuban Missile Crisis was a 13-day confrontation between the United States and the Soviet Union over American ballistic missile deployments in Italy and Turkey and the consequent Soviet ballistic missile deployment in Cuba.\n- The Cuban Missile Crisis was also known as the October Crisis, the Caribbean Crisis, and the Missile Scare.\n- During its Coast Guard career, USCGC Barataria served in the Cuban Missile Crisis and the Vietnam War.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
